		"Implemented: src/host/commands/queue.ts takes /queue drop <n> (position in /queue's list) or /queue drop <inbox id>; the web × sends the id so a queue that changed meanwhile cannot shift the target. SlashCommand.record gets the session id, so history and other clients show '/queue drop <n>', never the id. 'drop' followed by one word is now reserved like 'next' and 'clear'.",
